{
  "synthetic": true,
  "disclaimer": "SYNTHETIC: a fake summariser and a fake lexical judge. Measures navigation mechanics on a planted tree, not Jev, real summary quality, or real judgement.",
  "config": {
    "seed": 2,
    "n": 256,
    "facts": 12
  },
  "viewLines": 16,
  "viewLinesWithTopic": 5,
  "summarizerPolicy": [
    "Node budget 256 bytes; view budget 4096 bytes; every leaf and every merge goes through the summariser.",
    "A summary is one line `topics: <phrases> | themes: <words> |`, padded with dots to 132 bytes. It never contains a digit, so no value survives any level.",
    "A leaf (one message) keeps the topic phrase it states, whatever its value.",
    "A merged line covering 2^L messages keeps a child's topic only while L <= that fact's keep (seeded, 1..5). Old facts under coarse view lines are dropped from the view, and only zoom or chat_search can reach them.",
    "Over the node budget, a merge drops its earliest-listed topics first. Themes: the first 3 vocabulary words, interleaved."
  ],
  "countingRules": [
    "Agent steps: zoom, chat_search, chat_recall calls, budget 24 per probe. A beam is one script step. The prefetch gate adds no step.",
    "Judge calls: every call to the judge, by any component. Zoom calls: every memory.zoom call, gate and script included.",
    "Bytes: UTF-8 bytes the agent receives (tool results, the prefetch block, the script's printed output). The view is already in the prompt and is not counted.",
    "Found: the bytes received contain the fact's value. Probe question: names the topic, never the value."
  ],
